  "id": "10473",
  "self": "https://simeoncalixte1990.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10473",
  "key": "AIN-150",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[Settings] Organize settings into XDS collapsible subsections",
    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "User request (2026-11-06): separate Settings into subsections using the standard XDS section component."
            }
          ],
          "attrs": {
            "localId": "8e3ecc77f7d2"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "User story: As an individual or organization administrator, I want clearly labeled, independently expandable settings subsections so I can find and manage the relevant configuration without scrolling through unrelated forms. Reuse the existing settings workflows and AIN-138 user story; this task supplements AIN-140 and does not replace its broader obligations."
            }
          ],
          "attrs": {
            "localId": "f138216bb603"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Scope / source map: EnsuredUI/src/Pages/InsurerDashboard/Settings.tsx currently renders ModelLibrary, OrganizationCapabilitiesSettings and SubmissionReferenceSettings consecutively. Reuse the exported XDS CollapsibleSection from EnsuredXDS/src/components/CollapsibleSection.tsx (already used in SubjectInsuranceSection and SubjectTemplateFields). Use XDS tokens and its controlled collapsed/onToggle API; do not build a parallel custom accordion. SectionHeader is a heading primitive, not a substitute for the standard section container."
            }
          ],
          "attrs": {
            "localId": "594242ec8c00"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Acceptance criteria:"
            }
          ],
          "attrs": {
            "localId": "b784c876f6db"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "orderedList",
          "attrs": {
            "order": 1,
            "localId": "a988ae7e73af"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "attrs": {
                "localId": "48c64cf878b2"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Settings has three clearly labeled subsections: AI Models, Organization capabilities, and Submission contract references. Each uses the standard XDS CollapsibleSection with concise descriptive text and consistent spacing, headings and responsive styling."
                    }
                  ],
                  "attrs": {
                    "localId": "9cacebcdb76e"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "attrs": {
                "localId": "3baccd731a8b"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Sections expand/collapse independently via pointer and keyboard, expose correct aria-expanded state, and have visible focus. Avoid duplicate page-level titles or nested action buttons inside the section toggle. Keep all existing workflows reachable."
                    }
                  ],
                  "attrs": {
                    "localId": "72fd81307fb3"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "attrs": {
                "localId": "c30ed1e30bde"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Collapse/reopen preserves unsaved drafts, selected records, scope and relevant status. Current CollapsibleSection unmounts children when collapsed: explicitly solve state preservation by lifting state or a backward-compatible shared component enhancement; do not lose API keys being entered or trigger accidental saves/tests. Initial open/closed state is deliberate and covered by tests."
                    }
                  ],
                  "attrs": {
                    "localId": "2ef49cacda49"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "attrs": {
                "localId": "70d828624592"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Preserve permissions and all current save/test/default/inheritance/removal behavior. Show only actual saved model records; do not seed providers or choose unknown defaults. No backend configuration, credential, authorization or data-model changes required for presentation regrouping."
                    }
                  ],
                  "attrs": {
                    "localId": "816997948569"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "attrs": {
                "localId": "ab0d3723d3f6"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Executable Storybook play stories cover section toggling, independent state, keyboard/focus, draft preservation, observable save results and exact submitted payloads; include loading, empty, error/retry, permission and narrow-screen states. Use synthetic transports and block accidental application writes. Retain existing component and API/database regressions. If XDS changes, add shared-component regressions."
                    }
                  ],
                  "attrs": {
                    "localId": "3ef10ef5ad8c"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "attrs": {
                "localId": "5459b55830c9"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Verify the integrated Settings page at desktop and 375px without horizontal overflow; record ticket -> component -> story IDs -> commands/results in Jira and TASK_HANDOFF.md before Done."
                    }
                  ],
                  "attrs": {
                    "localId": "08edb07b1ec5"
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Related work: AIN-138 / AIN-140 own model settings behavior; AIN-143 chat connection behavior must not regress. Existing provider-access/staging gates remain open and are not prerequisites for arranging the settings sections. Exclude new providers, financial workflows, unrelated settings features and production rollout."
            }
          ],
          "attrs": {
            "localId": "55fe2ea0f6ba"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Task creation only: implementation has not started."
            }
          ],
          "attrs": {
            "localId": "398368537f15"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
